<tr><td colspan=2><font face='Tahoma,Arial,Helvetica' size=2>err, i was under the impression that they were just getting rid of hand held concs, which is a bloody good idea. conc jumping in qwtf required a LOT more skill in terms of placement and timing than poxy tfc conc jumping, and handheld conc jumping is one of the reasons that tfc is so poor. the other reason is the stupidly large damage that grenades do - in particular mirv grenades. then there's the whole half-life netcode/engine thing - i get < 20 fps at 512x384 halflife tfc on a g200 (yes, ive tried tweaking the hell out of it), and always > 35 512x384 in quake3fortress, and i don't really think i have to say anything about hl's netcode.</font></td></tr>
