<center>
<table align=center width='98%' border=0 bgcolor='#006699' cellpadding=3 cellspacing=2>
<tr><td><font face='Tahoma,Arial,Helvetica' size=2><b>Comentario por: </b><a href='mailto:rent_a_hero@hotbot.com'>Rent_A_Hero</a></td><td align=right><font face='Tahoma,Arial,Helvetica' size=2><b>Fecha:</b> 11 de Mayo de 2000, 08:56:45 pm</td></tr>
<tr><td colspan=2><font face='Tahoma,Arial,Helvetica' size=2>Now, what are Conc Grenades for?  They are to temporaraly get the enemy's fire off a weaker class's (scout, medic both have low hp/armor) ass.  Now I always thought that TFC was supposed to be a team game, in which only a very well balanced team could succesfuly charge into an enemy base, recover the key, and bring it home.  With the improper use of the Conc grenades, ANY old joe (yeah, anyone can use a script) is able to jump past the whole enemy encampment, grab the key, fly back, and grab 10 easy, gready points.  Now I think the idea of making the grenades weaker kicks ass, but heres a somewhat better Idea-  Make the force of the grenades only affect classes other than the Scout/Medic.  This way, people will be forced to play as a team to use the conc grenade, which would be just fine...If you guys love the conc grenade so much, this will be a great alternative, now well just see if your too greedy and want the 10 points for yourself instead of helping your team win.....
  - Rent A Hero -</font></td></tr>
</table>
</center><br>
